       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/6089a594bb0b0500707c78d8/e0c89ba4-1407-406d-af50-dc665f216277/32",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/6089a594bb0b0500707c78d8/e0c89ba4-1407-406d-af50-dc665f216277/48"
      },
      "displayName": "Dan Field",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a594bb0b0500707c78d8",
      "timeZone": "Europe/London"
     },
     "body": "<p>Just copying that comment here for readability:</p>\n\n<p>One Fedora 7 server behavior change surfaced by the integration tests, which<br/>\nclient users should be aware of:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><tt>PATCH</tt> <b>responses no longer carry the updated</b> <tt>ETag</tt><b>.</b> Against Fedora 6,<br/>\nthe <tt>ETag</tt> header on a successful <tt>PATCH</tt> response reflected the new state<br/>\nof the resource. Against Fedora 7.0.0 it reflects the state prior to the<br/>\nupdate. If you need the post-update <tt>ETag</tt> (e.g. for optimistic locking with<br/>\n<tt>If-Match</tt>), issue a fresh <tt>HEAD</tt>/<tt>GET</tt> after the <tt>PATCH</tt>.</li>\n</ul>\n",
     "created": "13/Jul/26 7:22 AM",
     "id": "28967",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/17058/comment/28967",
